 "summary": "Both prior findings are addressed: the subject-free four-vector lemmas now live in Lorentz.Vector (BasicExtensions/MinkowskiProductExtensions), the sqrt and artanh-domain helpers are public in their canonical mirrored homes, and the remaining rapidity-sum glue is two public named lemmas rather than an API gap. The rapidity definition carries a complete characteristic API (def, unit-direction, junk values, tanh uniqueness, exp/log, transverse-mass forms) with no exposed bodies and annotations consistent with the file's existing non-simp convention for component lemmas; note that the PR description advertises five `_add_` two-vector rapidity lemmas that do not exist in the file.",
